WEBVTT

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:09.880
I send you my greetings, Elder Sister.

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:13.750
It has been four months since I left Japan.

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:19.330
In answer to a request from Lord Horikawa himself,
I am acting as a spy in London.

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:23.880
Oh, a "spy" is something like an onmitsu or a ninja.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.500
Morning comes late for a spy.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:30.380
We often work deep into the night,
so we are much like owls.

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:34.790
I wonder why Westerners sleep
so high off of the ground.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.250
And they don't remove their footwear
when they come inside.

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:40.290
This makes their feet stink.

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:42.790
S-something stinks!

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:44.790
This girl is Beatrice.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.920
She is the daughter of a baron,
and she and I are in the same year at school.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:49.670
What is this smell?!

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:51.000
It's you, isn't it?!

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:53.500
How rude! I bathe every day-

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:54.960
That's not what I meant!

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:57.080
You brought something in here, didn't you?

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:59.210
Last time it was those rotten beans...

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:01.540
Oh, do you mean my natto?

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:04.000
What is it now? Meat?

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.460
Or is it fish?

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:06.830
Vegetables.

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:08.830
We call it nukazuke.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.080
It is delicious.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:48.330
All the students in the dormitories eat breakfast together.

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:49.790
But...

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:57.750
To be honest, the food of this nation is not very good.

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:08.790
At eight in the morning, class begins.

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:22.670
Miss Todo.

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:25.080
Answer this question.

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:29.290
I just haven't learned English very well yet.

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:31.250
It's true.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:33.790
Nine o'clock.

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:36.210
Time for training. They call it "physical education."

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:58.000
Physical exertion is my strongest suit.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:02.670
Ten o'clock. Music.

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:07.710
Today I demonstrated an instrument from Japan.

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:10.130
That is to say...

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.170
It's the only instrument I can play.

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:14.460
Eleven o'clock.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:15.920
Art.

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:25.790
(Sneak, sneak, sneak...)

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:29.670
Excuse me! That's going too far!

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:31.250
It was not well received.
Excuse me! That's going too far!

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:34.830
Twelve o'clock. Time for a midday break.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:38.170
We all leave the classroom and spend our time freely.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:41.330
What's that?

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:43.540
Fencing.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:47.250
Whoever hits their opponent
above the waist with a sabre wins.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:48.960
Western swordplay?

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:49.920
Fascinating.

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:51.500
Miss Chise, wait!

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:52.880
Many pardons!

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:55.170
What? You want to join the team?

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:57.420
I wish to contend with you.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:59.380
Contend?

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:02.130
If you mean a fencing match,
you'll need to issue a formal request.

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:03.670
Formal request?

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.170
Oh, yes!

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:07.580
I've heard of this! I happen to have one with me.

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:11.960
Disgusting!

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:13.790
What are you doing, Miss Chise?

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:14.500
Yuck!

00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:15.420
What?

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:18.040
I had heard that, in the West, when requesting
a contest of different martial arts,

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:20.130
you throw a white turnip at your opponent.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.420
That's for a duel!

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.710
And you don't throw turnips; you throw gloves!

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:25.000
Is that so?

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:26.460
I beg your pardon.

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:28.920
I did feel that something wasn't quite right.

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:29.880
Forgive me.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:32.210
I shall return to throw a glove at-

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.080
What is wrong with you?!

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:35.210
I've had enough of this!

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:37.040
Masks are acceptable, as well?

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.380
Then to a fair fight.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:39.960
Have at you!

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:41.130
I'm not dueling you!

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:43.580
This can't be happening.

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:44.580
Two different fighting styles!

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:45.960
Captain! You can do it!

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:48.040
You little-!

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:50.170
Hey! What are you doing!

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:53.960
Ladies! Stop it this instant!

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:03.420
Then you just defeated Professor Krauss?

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:04.540
I love it!

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:06.790
This is no laughing matter!

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:09.540
We eat our midday meal outside.

00:06:09.670 --> 00:06:12.580
It is a stylish affair in these parts, known as "lunch".

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:14.290
It serves him right.

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:16.920
That Krauss always had a dirty look in his eye.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:20.380
This is the leader of our band of spies, Dorothy.

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:21.880
She has a positive personality.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.170
Her alias is 17 years of age, but...

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:26.880
Oops.

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:29.790
...I must say it is quite a stretch.

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:32.040
You do be standing out too much, Miss Chise.

00:06:32.210 --> 00:06:35.830
You only just transferred here.
You shouldn't attract so much attention.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:37.330
This is Ange.

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:39.380
She talks like a bumpkin, but that is only an act.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:42.130
This woman tells lies constantly.

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.380
I apologize. I shall be careful in the future.

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:49.580
You're in an unfamiliar country. It can't be helped.

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:52.750
In fact, I think it would be more unnatural
if she blended in.

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:55.080
That... may be so.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:55.960
See?

00:06:55.960 --> 00:06:57.540
This is the princess of this nation.

00:06:57.670 --> 00:07:00.170
She is even more of a mystery than Ange.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:04.130
Why would the princess of one kingdom
act as a spy for an enemy country?

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:08.250
And is she not afraid to cross such a perilous bridge?

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:09.830
What is it?

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:12.790
You are always smiling.

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:14.830
Does it look fake?

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:16.130
No...

00:07:16.130 --> 00:07:17.040
It's alright.

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:21.250
People always tell me they can't
figure out what I'm thinking.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:23.080
Nothing is wrong with you!

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:26.250
You're just too perfect at everything,
Your Highness.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:29.330
But you might say it's hard
to tell how you really feel.

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:34.080
When she pinches her collar, that's the sign
that she needs to tell us about a mission.

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:38.290
Princess has bodyguards surrounding her
even at school.

00:07:38.710 --> 00:07:43.250
And one of them reports on her activities
to the Home Secretary.

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:50.880
The lavatory is the ideal spot for clandestine meetings.

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:53.250
Oh, Princess. How do you do?

00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:56.080
How do you do, Miss Lily?

00:07:57.750 --> 00:07:59.210
Lily Gaveston.

00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:01.380
The daughter of the Kingdom's Chief Justice.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:04.330
She, too, is one of the Home Secretary's collaborators.

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:06.630
She has not been trained as a spy...

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:09.170
But she is the same sex as Princess,
and in the same class.

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:11.420
This actually makes her the bigger nuisance.

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:15.210
I see you're with the Natural History Club again today.

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:17.920
G-good afternoon, Miss Lily.

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:18.960
Good afternoon.

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:20.250
And who are you?

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:21.750
I-I'm Ange.

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:27.170
Oh, I'm so sorry. I just can't remember
the names of people I don't associate with.

00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:28.500
How unsightly.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:32.670
If you dislike Ange, you would do well
to come out and say it.

00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:36.290
Your senseless sarcasm
diminishes the quality of your character.

00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:40.380
Princess.

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:43.290
I think you should choose your friends with more care.

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:47.080
But I thought of you as a friend.

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.130
Are you saying I should reconsider?

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:53.130
Th-things are fine the way they are!

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:59.960
When we carry out our spy work,
we use this underground passage.

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:07.540
There are so many cars,

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:08.830
and airships.

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:11.670
You would never behold such a sight in Japan.

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:15.420
Big, tall buildings, like castles, line the streets.

00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:19.960
When I go into town, I cannot avoid
the painful reminder of how different our nations are.

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:27.960
Yes, please tell the Master that his wife
wishes him to stop by Piccadilly Circus.

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:28.580
Beatrice's throat is equipped with advanced technology
that can mimic any human voice.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:29.460
Beatrice's throat is equipped with advanced technology
that can mimic any human voice.
Yes.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:30.080
Beatrice's throat is equipped with advanced technology
that can mimic any human voice.

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:32.710
Beatrice's throat is equipped with advanced technology
that can mimic any human voice.
Yes. Excuse me.

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:33.960
Beatrice's throat is equipped with advanced technology
that can mimic any human voice.

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:38.460
She herself is good with machines,
which makes her a reliable ally.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.330
We were right.

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:42.830
The president of the Privy Council WILL be there.

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:43.880
Will they?

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:47.420
Now all we have to do is find out
what their secret meeting is about.

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:51.330
Rain.

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:53.540
Perfect. I can use it to my advantage.

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:56.630
Dear Sister.

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:58.880
That is known as "a woman's weapon".

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:02.580
Unfortunately, it's one I have yet to acquire.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:04.290
Oh, no!

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:05.920
Where is this rain coming from?

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:08.880
Well, I'll go in from the roof.

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:10.750
Chise, you're on standby.

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:13.630
There is surprisingly little for me to do.

00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:17.250
Ange says it's better that way, but...

00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:31.000
Isn't it only natural that I should want to be useful,

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:32.920
as a member of the team?

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:42.170
I have regular interviews with Lord Horikawa.

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:47.630
Delicious!

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:50.040
This kintsuba is exquisite!

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:52.500
I had it sent here from the capital.

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:54.750
Of course. The capital.

00:10:56.830 --> 00:10:58.000
Of course it's so good!

00:10:58.130 --> 00:10:59.250
By the way, Chise.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.540
What do you think of Princess?

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:03.380
Dear Sister.

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:07.170
My task is to investigate the Commonwealth.

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:10.250
In other words, I am spying on the spies.

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:13.670
I have determined her to be a clever, resolute woman.

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:15.250
Will it succeed?

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:17.710
This "Operation: Changeling".

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:20.750
I have only been with them a fortnight.

00:11:21.330 --> 00:11:23.750
I would like more time to form a proper judgment.

00:11:24.790 --> 00:11:26.960
I hope you don't think me a coward, Chise.

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:29.080
Our nation is still small.

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:31.750
Of the Kingdom and the Commonwealth,

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:37.420
we must determine which horse will win the race
and ride it, or we will have no future.

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:39.960
Understood.

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:47.920
Please, do not worry, Dear Sister.

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:51.960
I promise I will find the information
that will benefit our nation.

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:54.040
I will be useful.

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:01.750
It is funny because it is so fitting.

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:05.380
This IS a place where chrysalides
emerge into adulthood.

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:07.040
She's a commoner, isn't she?

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:09.170
Obviously she's after the money.

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:11.710
Hey. Out of our way.

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:14.500
Oriental.

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.250
Don't you speak English?

00:12:17.790 --> 00:12:20.670
This butterfly is about to leave its cocoon.

00:12:21.210 --> 00:12:24.040
If you were not all spread across the path,

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:26.210
you could easily pass behind me.

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:27.790
Indeed.

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:30.130
That's one way to do it, or...

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:34.880
Now there's no reason for you to stay there.

00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:37.670
That's my big brother. So logical.

00:12:38.710 --> 00:12:39.750
You villains.

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:42.130
I'll let you in on something, Oriental.

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:44.290
That chrysalid represents all of you.

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:47.420
You lot had better behave yourselves
until you get your own wings.

00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:49.920
Do you think they even CAN get wings?

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:53.420
When a man speaks too much, he appears a fool.

00:12:53.420 --> 00:12:54.580
What?

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:01.000
I challenge you to a duel!

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:06.170
You will atone for the crimes of insulting
my homeland and stamping out a small life!

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:08.210
What? What are you on about?

00:13:08.210 --> 00:13:09.960
Just ignore her, Brother.

00:13:09.960 --> 00:13:11.380
I am serious!

00:13:11.580 --> 00:13:12.290
Chise?

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:13.710
Looks like she's gotten into a fight.

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:15.040
Not again, Miss Chise!

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:19.170
Stop it. A duel is a fight to defend one's honor.

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:23.420
No one would stake his honor
on a fight with an oriental girl.

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:25.420
What are you doing, Miss Chise?

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:27.630
I am preparing to duel this knave!

00:13:27.630 --> 00:13:28.500
Miss Chise!

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:29.460
Don't do it!

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:31.250
It's too dreadful, so it is!

00:13:31.380 --> 00:13:32.420
But...

00:13:32.630 --> 00:13:33.750
A duel?

00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:35.710
That's hardly a peaceful solution.

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:36.920
Princess.

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:40.000
Well, well. So you were a friend of the princess.

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:42.170
I'm not interested in a duel.

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:45.630
It was your little oriental friend who wanted to fight.

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:47.750
But you gave me reason to!

00:13:47.750 --> 00:13:49.580
Stop it, Miss Chise!

00:13:50.130 --> 00:13:51.580
Have you forgotten your duty?

00:13:51.580 --> 00:13:53.290
Learn to pick your battles!

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:58.460
I have no intention of embarrassing
one of Princess' friends.

00:13:58.670 --> 00:13:59.670
Let's go.

00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:06.040
Chise.

00:14:06.040 --> 00:14:08.000
Spies don't attract attention.

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:09.540
I apologize.

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:20.290
Dear Sister, I've done it again.

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:23.000
Come in.

00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:28.460
I can tell by the look on your face
that you didn't expect to see me.

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:29.330
Oh.

00:14:29.330 --> 00:14:31.080
I apologize for my behavior earlier.

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:33.420
Ange and the others must be appalled.

00:14:33.420 --> 00:14:34.790
That's true.

00:14:34.960 --> 00:14:37.710
Have you come to reprimand me?

00:14:37.710 --> 00:14:39.790
No, quite the opposite.

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:44.750
I've come to teach you our country's rules for dueling.

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:45.750
What?

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:49.130
There's more to it than throwing a white glove.

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:52.580
To start, you need someone to act as Second.

00:14:52.880 --> 00:14:55.000
The role of whom is to negotiate
with the other party's Second

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:58.250
to determine the date, time,
and method of the duel.

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:02.790
You'll also need to prepare a witness and a doctor.

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:05.710
You must choose a location
where there won't be many people.

00:15:05.710 --> 00:15:06.250
And-

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:06.830
Wait.

00:15:06.830 --> 00:15:07.750
Stop a moment!

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:10.500
Were you not opposed to dueling?

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:14.170
There are times when a person has to fight.

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:17.420
If you're going to do it, you absolutely must win.

00:15:17.420 --> 00:15:19.540
Do you understand, Miss Chise?

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:23.080
Allow me to review the rules.

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:25.250
You will stand ten paces from each other,

00:15:25.250 --> 00:15:28.540
and fire three shots from your pistols.

00:15:29.170 --> 00:15:33.380
Mr. Cameron, the challenged party,
has asked to go second.

00:15:33.670 --> 00:15:37.040
You will take turns, with Miss Chise firing first.

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:39.460
The first to injure the other wins.

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:42.960
Should all six shots miss, bygones will be bygones.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:44.380
You both agree?

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:46.540
Of course, Princess.

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:47.670
I have no objections.

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:51.290
I've prepared some Robert Wogdon dueling pistols.

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:53.500
For your approval.

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:57.000
In a duel, fairness is valued above all.

00:15:57.330 --> 00:16:00.500
That is why we each use the same weapons.

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:13.880
N-now, I, Lily Gaveston,
of the Gaveston Law Lord bloodline,

00:16:13.880 --> 00:16:17.000
will stand as witness to the outcome of this duel.

00:16:17.130 --> 00:16:19.250
Will both parties please take your marks.

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:24.500
A witness is chosen who is not aligned with either side.

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:27.250
Still, there was no need to choose HER.

00:16:28.080 --> 00:16:29.250
That's far enough.

00:16:30.540 --> 00:16:32.500
Hey, Oriental! Can you shoot a gun?

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:34.170
I wouldn't blame you for crying.

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:36.210
Kung-fu isn't allowed, after all.

00:16:37.250 --> 00:16:38.130
Dear Sister.

00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:41.750
The people here know nothing of the land of Japan.

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:45.420
It's sad, I suppose, that this is where our country stands.

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:47.250
The Seconds will come to order.

00:16:48.130 --> 00:16:49.250
Ready...

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:50.580
Begin!

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:55.290
They deliberately use old-fashioned guns,
to make it difficult to hit our targets.

00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:59.920
I am told this is because otherwise, differing levels of skill
would make the contest unfair.

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:17.040
It IS an old gun.

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:18.630
These things happen.

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:20.630
Isn't that right, Witness?

00:17:20.630 --> 00:17:22.210
What? But...

00:17:22.210 --> 00:17:25.210
Or can you prove that the gun has been tampered with?

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:26.710
Well...

00:17:26.830 --> 00:17:27.960
My turn.

00:17:28.130 --> 00:17:30.170
Here I go, oriental woman.

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:33.920
Miss Chise!

00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:38.380
Dear Sister, this is what THEY call "fair".

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:40.670
I do have two shots left.

00:17:40.670 --> 00:17:42.670
So let's see you quaking in your boots.

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:48.500
Now it is my turn, correct?

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:52.210
Don't tell me you're going to THROW the bullet at me?

00:17:52.790 --> 00:17:53.920
Indeed I am.

00:18:00.040 --> 00:18:00.880
Brother!

00:18:01.920 --> 00:18:02.630
Brother!

00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:03.580
Damn her!

00:18:04.630 --> 00:18:05.880
Witness!

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:08.040
W-we have a winner!

00:18:08.330 --> 00:18:09.420
In accordance with the rules-

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:12.250
Wait! You can't possibly count that magic trick!

00:18:12.380 --> 00:18:13.380
Keep going!

00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:15.500
Y-yeah! This duel isn't over!

00:18:15.670 --> 00:18:17.290
Make it fair, Witness!

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:18.500
B-but...

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:19.920
I will continue.

00:18:20.460 --> 00:18:22.380
If you wish to go on, then fire.

00:18:22.380 --> 00:18:25.710
However, on my next turn,
I will aim between the eyebrows.

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:28.290
Enough!

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:29.880
You win, Oriental!

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:31.830
Can't you hear me?

00:18:31.830 --> 00:18:33.960
Ruddy bumpkin doesn't even know the rules of dueling!

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:37.080
Mr. Cameron, your apology!

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:48.040
Alright!

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:49.040
I'm sorry!

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:52.580
I apologize for insulting your country,
and I take back everything I said!

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:56.670
Challenger! Do you accept the apology?

00:19:03.420 --> 00:19:04.420
Doctor!

00:19:04.420 --> 00:19:05.330
See to my brother.

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:06.710
R-right away!

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:10.040
Don't crowd me! You're so annoying!

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:12.210
Don't push yourself.

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:13.500
Here, hold on to me.

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:15.330
It's nothing! I'm fine.

00:19:15.710 --> 00:19:16.420
Let's go!

00:19:17.580 --> 00:19:19.830
Well done, Miss Chise.

00:19:20.290 --> 00:19:22.880
They didn't come.

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:23.500
What?

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:24.830
Never mind.

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:27.210
It is nothing.

00:19:32.380 --> 00:19:34.540
What do you think of Operation: Changeling?

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:38.000
We last spoke a mere week ago.

00:19:38.130 --> 00:19:40.580
The plan will not progress so immediately.

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:43.960
Regardless, I would like to hear your thoughts.

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:48.330
The Kingdom is pressuring us to settle this treaty.

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:54.170
I would like to use your information
to help me determine whether to accept their terms.

00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:57.000
I...

00:20:03.710 --> 00:20:04.920
Where were you?

00:20:05.210 --> 00:20:06.540
We're having a meeting.

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:07.960
Understood.

00:20:19.250 --> 00:20:20.500
Princess?

00:20:21.540 --> 00:20:23.330
Isn't anyone here?

00:20:39.330 --> 00:20:41.330
Miss Chise, congratulations!

00:20:41.580 --> 00:20:43.540
East side!

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:45.670
Congratulations, Miss Chise!

00:20:45.670 --> 00:20:47.630
West side!

00:20:47.880 --> 00:20:48.750
What is this?

00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:50.250
What are you doing?

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:52.210
Dohyo iri.

00:20:52.420 --> 00:20:53.130
Huh?

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:59.670
I heard that when a samurai wins a duel,
this is how they celebrate.

00:20:59.670 --> 00:21:02.170
This is how they do things in Japan, right?

00:21:02.880 --> 00:21:05.420
It's, um... very unique.

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:10.290
Do you like it, then?

00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:14.170
I see Japan is still an unknown nation to the people here.

00:21:14.170 --> 00:21:17.130
Forget Japan, YOU'RE the special one.

00:21:17.130 --> 00:21:18.500
Troublemaker.

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:21.080
You attract a lot of attention for a spy.

00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:25.040
But it felt great when you talked back
to Lily in the lavatory.

00:21:25.330 --> 00:21:29.500
Besides, it's thanks to you
that our mission went so smoothly.

00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:34.920
That's right. I saw no problems with Princess today.

00:21:35.080 --> 00:21:36.540
Yes, that's right.

00:21:36.920 --> 00:21:40.880
While you were off having your duel,
we snuck into Lily's room.

00:21:40.880 --> 00:21:44.210
Sure enough, she was hiding a direct telephone line.

00:21:44.330 --> 00:21:46.790
We took the liberty of tinkering with it, just a little.

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:50.330
Is that why you weren't present at the duel?

00:21:50.880 --> 00:21:52.250
Anything unusual?

00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:55.040
Maybe all the hullabaloo about a duel.

00:21:55.170 --> 00:21:58.210
I told you about that weird oriental runt.

00:21:58.330 --> 00:22:00.330
Are you gonna take that from her, Chise?

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:04.380
If you ask me, everyone here is a weird Westerner.

00:22:04.540 --> 00:22:08.000
Well, not as weird as the Black Lizard girl over there.

00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:09.460
I'm normal.

00:22:09.580 --> 00:22:13.080
I'm not so desperate to be in secondary school
that I would hide my age.

00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:14.960
I told you it's part of the mission!

00:22:15.170 --> 00:22:17.130
Besides, I can still pull it off!

00:22:17.250 --> 00:22:18.290
With enough makeup.

00:22:18.420 --> 00:22:20.330
I'm only three years older than you!

00:22:24.330 --> 00:22:26.500
Lord Horikawa, I hereby report.

00:22:26.670 --> 00:22:30.580
In all honesty, I do not know
if Operation: Changeling is possible.

00:22:30.960 --> 00:22:31.960
However...

00:22:34.670 --> 00:22:39.130
What I do know is... I want them to be victorious.
